WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
WebSSH. Your servers. Your browser. Your rules. A self-hosted SSH and SFTP workspace. This walkthrough uses example data.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:12.000
An SSH terminal shows service status, disk capacity and the current user on an example host.

3
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:22.000
The operator selects a second session in the pane assignment dialog. Two terminal panes show separate example hosts.

4
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:28.000
The SFTP File Manager displays two sources side by side. The operator selects README.md.

5
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:38.000
The file preview opens. The operator enters edit mode and adds a release-validation checklist item. The edit is marked unsaved.

6
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:49.000
The Commands workspace opens a saved command set. The operator searches for Disk Usage and adds it as a third step.

7
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:55.000
Back in the terminal workspace, the operator adds the next deployment task to the personal notepad.

8
00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Bring your own servers. Start locally with Docker. Get WebSSH at getwebssh.com. Free and open source under the MIT license.
